#===============================================================================
# Tandem Tales Agent (Python) Environment Variables
#===============================================================================
# These values define important properties of your agent that the Tandem Tales
# server uses to identify it.

# *** Agent Name ***
# This is the keyword used by the server to refer to your agent. It can only
# contain letters, digits, and underscores. It can be a maximum of 20 characters
# long. If your agent's name is hard-coded in your source code, make sure it
# matches this value.
name="Salience"

# *** Agent Password ***
# This is the password your agent will give when it attempts to connect to the
# server. Whether your agent requires a password depends on how the Tandem Tales
# server is configured. A password guarantees that only your agent can use the
# above name and prevents other agents from pretending to be your agent.
# Passwords should always be read from an environment variable and should never
# be hard-coded into your agent's source code. When other people run your agent,
# they might give it a different password in their Tandem Tales database, so
# by reading it from the environment you ensure your agent can still connect
# without needing to modify your code.
password="dummy"

# *** Agent Title ***
# This is a short title given to your agent on the Tandem Tales website. It
# should be one or a few words. Each word should be capitalized.
title="Salient"

# *** Agent Description ***
# This is a description given to your agent on the Tandem Tales website. It
# should be about one or two sentences.
description="An agent that makes salient choices."

# *** Story World ***
# When you visit the local Tandem Tales web server running on http://localhost,
# the homepage will have a link to play a game with your agent. If you set this
# variable, that game will use this story world. If your agent is only designed
# to handle one story would, you should set this variable to that world's name.
# world="tutorial"

# *** Role ***
# If you set this variable, the link at http://localhost will give your agent
# this role in the story. If your agent is only designed to play one role, you
# should set this variable to one of the two roles below.
# role="PLAYER"
# role="GAME_MASTER"

# *** External API Key ***
# Your agent can use an external API for expensive operations like text
# embedding and chat completion, but you will need an API key, which is like
# a user name and password all in one. Currently, Tandem Tales uses the
# OpenRouter.ai API, so you will need an API key from that website.
# !!! WARNING !!!
# If you set this value, DO NOT commit this file to a public repository like
# GitHub.com or send this file to others. If someone else sees your API key,
# they can spend money on your account. If you are sending your agent to someone
# else to run, do not include your key. They should provide their own key.
# apikey=your-key-here